## Usage

```bash
pip install {{ distribution_name }}
```

```yaml
my_project:
  target: dev
  outputs:
    dev:
      type: polars
      catalogs:
        - name: my_catalog
          type: {{ catalog_name }}
          schema: dev
```

## Development

1. Implement the methods in `{{ package_name }}/catalog.py` and add your profile options to `{{ class_prefix }}CatalogConfig`.
2. Fill in `PRIMARY_CATALOG_OPTIONS` and `SECONDARY_CATALOG_OPTIONS` in `tests/conftest.py`: two test instances of your backend that don't share storage.
3. Run the tests:

   ```bash
   uv run pytest -n auto
   ```

   `tests/test_catalog.py` calls the catalog directly, `tests/test_dbt.py` runs dbt projects against it.

Test schemas are removed by the `cleanup_test_schemas` fixture in `tests/conftest.py`: at the end of a run, and for leftovers of earlier runs older than 24 hours. Check that it works for your backend.

See [Custom catalogs](https://github.com/datamindedbe/incubator-dbt-polars/blob/main/docs/guides/custom-catalog.md) for the catalog API.

## Release

Set `version` in `pyproject.toml`, then push a matching tag (`v0.1.0`). `.github/workflows/publish.yml` publishes to PyPI with trusted publishing.

## Template updates

This project was generated from the [dbt-polars catalog template](https://github.com/datamindedbe/incubator-dbt-polars/tree/main/catalog-template). To pull in template updates:

```bash
uvx copier update
```
